            <ArticleTitle>[Bochdalek hernia: a rare cause of dyspnea and abdominal pain in adults].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1061-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present here a case of a sixty year old man with a symptomatic hernia of Bochdalek. Its diagnostic was long to be established because this type of congenital diaphragmatic hernia is rare and mainly occurs in neonates. However when looking at a patient with dyspnea and lasting atypical abdominal pain, such a diagnosis has to be looked for, even if such a clinical entity is extremely rare in adults.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
